  "fakemon": [
	{ "name": "Scorchick", "art_id": "Scorchick", "male_ratio": 0.5, "type": "Fire", "moves": ["squawk", "ignite", "peck", "mimic"], "learnset": [{"move": "squawk", "level": 1}, {"move": "ignite", "level": 2}, {"move": "peck", "level": 3}, {"move": "mimic", "level": 5}, {"move": "scratch", "level": 7}, {"move": "heat_up", "level": 12}, {"move": "singe", "level": 17}, {"move": "intercept", "level": 20}, {"move": "fire_charge", "level": 22}, {"move": "nest", "level": 25}, {"move": "fireheart", "level": 27}, {"move": "whirlwind", "level": 30}, {"move": "wingbeat", "level": 33}, {"move": "burn_off", "level": 36}, {"move": "skyfall", "level": 38}, {"move": "phoenix_charge", "level": 40}, {"move": "challenging_call", "level": 42}, {"move": "harsh_sunlight", "level": 45}, {"move": "inferno_plume", "level": 50}, {"move": "inner_focus", "level": 55}, {"move": "inferno", "level": 60}], "level": 5, "max_hp": 55, "attack": 70, "defense": 50, "special_attack": 40, "special_defense": 45, "speed": 50, "color": "e45b5b", "size": "0.6 m", "description": "A cheery rainforest Fakemon, Scorchick's feathers glow with heat. Their sweet natured personalities and strong verbal communication skills help them form close bonds with parents, trainers and other nest mates. Scorchick love spicy peppers, and can be a pest to growers that specialize in these fruits. It's thought that the capsaicin is related to the chemical reaction required to power their flames, which ignite the wings, tail and tuft of the Fakemon without harming the chick itself. Don't be deceived by the cute Fakemon however, the fires ignited are hot enough to melt iron.", "catch_rate": 75, "base_exp": 64 },
	{ "name": "Sylvafin", "art_id": "Sylvafin", "male_ratio": 0.5, "type": "Water", "moves": ["peck", "soak", "flutter", "photon_beam"], "learnset": [{"move": "peck", "level": 1}, {"move": "soak", "level": 2}, {"move": "flutter", "level": 3}, {"move": "photon_beam", "level": 5}, {"move": "flip_turn", "level": 7}, {"move": "discern", "level": 9}, {"move": "purify", "level": 13}, {"move": "fin_flash", "level": 15}, {"move": "aqua_jet", "level": 20}, {"move": "dazzle", "level": 23}, {"move": "brilliant_light", "level": 25}, {"move": "veil", "level": 27}, {"move": "disable", "level": 30}, {"move": "prayer", "level": 32}, {"move": "scald", "level": 35}, {"move": "smite", "level": 40}, {"move": "aureal_flood", "level": 45}, {"move": "remembrance", "level": 50}, {"move": "celestial_chorus", "level": 55}], "level": 5, "max_hp": 55, "attack": 35, "defense": 50, "special_attack": 65, "special_defense": 65, "speed": 40, "color": "5596e6", "size": "0.7 m", "description": "These rare and graceful Fakemon inhabit the warmest and most heavily planted bodies of water in the rainforest. Sylvafin carry themselves with a sense of dignity and grace - until it is feeding time. In this instance, they become quite the little beggars, forgetting to act the part of an elitist. Their scales reflect sunlight, and perhaps something deeper, causing the Fakemon to glow. It's methods baffle scientists, who have recently discovered that the source of the glow has nothing to do with bioluminescence, as if the source of the glow cannot be explained by the natural world alone. The trusting disposition and rarity of these Fakemon makes conducting any studies extremely unpopular with most people.", "catch_rate": 75, "base_exp": 64 },
	{ "name": "Keklid", "art_id": "Keklid", "male_ratio": null, "type": "Plant", "moves": ["petal_whip", "charm", "stare", "mind_wave"], "learnset": [{"move": "petal_whip", "level": 1}, {"move": "charm", "level": 2}, {"move": "stare", "level": 3}, {"move": "mind_wave", "level": 5}, {"move": "constrict", "level": 7}, {"move": "flutter", "level": 11}, {"move": "drain", "level": 13}, {"move": "remedy", "level": 15}, {"move": "vicegrip", "level": 17}, {"move": "mind_bolt", "level": 20}, {"move": "bloom", "level": 22}, {"move": "seed", "level": 25}, {"move": "regrow", "level": 28}, {"move": "mycelial_hunt", "level": 32}, {"move": "drain_toxin", "level": 35}, {"move": "rootmind", "level": 37}, {"move": "synaptic_bloom", "level": 40}, {"move": "hysteria", "level": 42}, {"move": "chlorophyll_cannon", "level": 45}, {"move": "vital_cognition", "level": 50}], "level": 5, "max_hp": 55, "attack": 35, "defense": 50, "special_attack": 70, "special_defense": 60, "speed": 40, "color": "55c878", "size": "0.5 m", "description": "A rare and wild wonder, Keklid require extremely precise temperatures, humidity and fungal conditions to germinate from tiny seeds. Such conditions can only exist in the deep lowland rainforests and only under a seed's exposure to a specific fungal host. Upon hatching however, they voraciously seek out fungal colonies to feast on mycelium. It's thought that the fungal networks not only power the flower's own metabolism, but that it also has the unusual effect of granting the Fakemon a type of non-animal cognition as well. These Fakemon are generally described as joyous, but fail to thrive in cooler or drier conditions.", "catch_rate": 75, "base_exp": 64 },
	{ "name": "Slumboth", "art_id": "Slumboth", "male_ratio": 0.5, "type": "Normal", "moves": ["doze_off", "sleep_talk", "defense_curl"], "learnset": [{"move": "doze_off", "level": 1}, {"move": "sleep_talk", "level": 2}, {"move": "defense_curl", "level": 5}, {"move": "scratch", "level": 7}, {"move": "gnaw", "level": 11}, {"move": "dream", "level": 13}, {"move": "punch", "level": 15, "evolution_move": true}, {"move": "counter", "level": 19}, {"move": "sleep_off", "level": 23}, {"move": "bulk_up", "level": 25}, {"move": "slash", "level": 27}, {"move": "snore", "level": 30}, {"move": "hammer_arm", "level": 35}, {"move": "sleep_swing", "level": 40}, {"move": "scourge", "level": 45}, {"move": "kinetic_pummel", "level": 50}, {"move": "rest", "level": 55}], "level": 5, "max_hp": 55, "attack": 45, "defense": 55, "special_attack": 25, "special_defense": 45, "speed": 20, "color": "9d8668", "size": "1.0 m", "description": "A lazy forest Fakemon that hangs in the canopy, waking only long enough to eat leaves. Its cushioned, insulated body protects it when it falls, though it would rather eat rotting leaves on the muddy floor than climb back up. Its warm, contented reputation is difficult to verify: official observations question whether Slumboth displays any recognizable personality.", "catch_rate": 200, "base_exp": 55 },
	{ "name": "Dartlet", "art_id": "Dartlet", "male_ratio": 0.5, "type": "Poison", "moves": ["poison_bubble", "croak", "leap"], "learnset": [{"move": "poison_bubble", "level": 1}, {"move": "croak", "level": 2}, {"move": "leap", "level": 5}, {"move": "poison_tongue", "level": 9}, {"move": "dartlet_stare", "level": 11}, {"move": "drain", "level": 13}, {"move": "incinerate", "level": 15, "evolution_move": true}, {"move": "cacophony", "level": 17}, {"move": "singe", "level": 19}, {"move": "warning_flare", "level": 23}, {"move": "coat_toxin", "level": 25}, {"move": "flashcroak", "level": 28}, {"move": "puff_up", "level": 30}, {"move": "flamethrower", "level": 35, "evolution_move": true}, {"move": "harsh_sunlight", "level": 40}, {"move": "alkaloid_mist", "level": 45}, {"move": "sun_chorus", "level": 50}, {"move": "toxic_flare", "level": 55}, {"move": "grand_display", "level": 60}], "level": 5, "max_hp": 50, "attack": 10, "defense": 35, "special_attack": 80, "special_defense": 35, "speed": 60, "color": "e45b8f", "size": "0.1 m", "description": "Dartlet are most often seen croaking contentedly after heavy rain. Their brilliant colors flash as they hop, warning other creatures of the toxins secreted through their skin. Their beauty and enormous eyes have made them popular with people—usually from a respectful distance. Dartlet are unusually well-tempered and readily approach patient Trainers, to the limited extent that they understand what training is. Even incidental contact with their poison remains hazardous, however. Healthy Dartlet constantly burn excess metabolic energy as heat, and become noticeably warm when excited. Their seemingly impossible metabolism continues to bewilder endocrinologists.", "catch_rate": 200, "base_exp": 60 },
	{ "name": "Skeeter", "art_id": "Skeeter", "male_ratio": 0.5, "type": "Bug", "moves": ["gnaw", "buzz", "needle_nip"], "learnset": [{"move": "gnaw", "level": 1}, {"move": "buzz", "level": 2}, {"move": "needle_nip", "level": 5}, {"move": "bite", "level": 7}, {"move": "infest", "level": 11}, {"move": "swoop", "level": 13}, {"move": "blood_draw", "level": 15}, {"move": "torment", "level": 17}, {"move": "evade", "level": 19}, {"move": "swarm", "level": 22}, {"move": "gather", "level": 25}, {"move": "leech_life", "level": 28}, {"move": "night_dart", "level": 32}, {"move": "hypnotic_hum", "level": 35}, {"move": "scourge", "level": 37}, {"move": "bloodmoon", "level": 41}, {"move": "plague", "level": 47}], "level": 5, "max_hp": 35, "attack": 40, "defense": 30, "special_attack": 45, "special_defense": 30, "speed": 60, "color": "57456f", "size": "0.01 m", "description": "Small flying Fakemon commonly found in huge numbers near still bodies of water. Its wings are weak, so it avoids winds stronger than a gentle breeze. When it bites larger Fakemon or people, it leaves behind an itchy bump. Skeeter seems to take particular delight in annoying larger beings and grows noticeably more aggressive after sunset. Its bites are often close together, and people or Fakemon bitten once are more likely to be bitten again. Surely this is only survival pressure and not malice. After all, a bug like this cannot willingly choose evil.", "catch_rate": 200, "base_exp": 55 }
	,{ "name": "Lochirp", "art_id": "Lochirp", "male_ratio": 0.5, "types": ["Plant", "Mystic"], "moves": ["nectar_drink", "petal_whip", "dazzle", "charm"], "learnset": [{"move": "nectar_drink", "level": 1}, {"move": "petal_whip", "level": 2}, {"move": "dazzle", "level": 3}, {"move": "charm", "level": 5}, {"move": "remedy", "level": 9}, {"move": "flutter", "level": 11}, {"move": "gust", "level": 14}, {"move": "bloom", "level": 16, "evolution_move": true}, {"move": "fey_dust", "level": 18}, {"move": "petalwake", "level": 21}, {"move": "mist", "level": 23}, {"move": "lotus_dart", "level": 26}, {"move": "magic_pulse", "level": 30}, {"move": "fey_gardens", "level": 33}, {"move": "solar_ray", "level": 36}, {"move": "lotus_absolution", "level": 40}, {"move": "mystic_stream", "level": 45}, {"move": "paradise_ray", "level": 50}, {"move": "paradise_bloom", "level": 55}], "level": 5, "max_hp": 40, "attack": 20, "defense": 30, "special_attack": 55, "special_defense": 50, "speed": 65, "color": "db7fc7", "size": "0.1 m", "description": "The presence of elusive Lochirp indicates a rainforest rich in healthy flowering plants. These tiny nectar-feeders scatter dust that stimulates new buds and sleep inside large flowers wrapped in petal-like plumage. Though widely imagined as gentle moon-blossom spirits, they are active by day and aggressively defend productive flowers, becoming fiercely loyal only to a small circle of trusted companions.", "catch_rate": 120, "base_exp": 60 }
  ]
}
